WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.420
Ninja Gaiden!

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:03.100
Ninja Action!

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:26.040
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.060
I'm Mike.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:28.160
And I'm Sean.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.360
And that's it?

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:30.680
That's it for today?

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:34.020
You would think, you would think it's a very important episode.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:35.360
I would think at least.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.180
So Sean, do you think this is an important episode?

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:49.540
It seems like it's a pretty important episode, but real quick, Mike, we just had a discussion about the pronunciation of the title of this game before we recorded, and you still said it weird.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:55.440
I feel like the only way to say this is in a way that like no one's ever heard it before.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:59.840
So this way you can't argue, you know, with the, the Gaiden or Gaiden fans.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:00.960
You just say Gaiden.

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:02.820
Gaiden! You know?

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:03.800
It's like French.

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:05.460
It's like French. It's Gaiden.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:09.500
Ninja Gaiden. Yeah.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:11.360
I love it. I like that.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:20.600
I think that's cool. Or we could just refer to it as Ninja Action, which is actually not quite on the back of the box, but it is two words on the back of the box.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:21.780
And that was the best I could pull from.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.460
It's the first two words on the back of the box.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:29.800
So you get what you get sometimes when it comes to the opening titles of a Nostalgia episode.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:34.300
Yeah. And the, the legacy of this game kind of precedes it.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:35.840
It, it does.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:48.660
It does. But I don't know about you, but when I think of this whole franchise, I imagine an incredibly difficult franchise that has honestly made me shy away from it over the last 30 years of my life.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.020
Absolutely. I'm, I'm right there with you.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:59.440
I, because of all of the horror stories I've heard about this game, it was sort of like a Ghosts and Goblins thing, but more people, I, I feel like.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:10.440
Uh, we're playing Ninja Gaiden more, um, or at least like games in this series more than Ghosts and Goblins more recently.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:14.900
Um, so I had some friends that played the more, like the modern versions.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.620
Uh, but even, even then I was like, no, thank you.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:22.640
I'd prefer to play a game that is, is a little less hard, even though I never really played.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:32.280
Yeah. In a way, the reputation of the reboot series on, uh, the Xbox, it, that to me was like before Dark Souls, that was Dark Souls.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:35.300
Like you just had this reputation of it being incredibly hard.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:38.460
And I was like, well, why would I, why would I buy a game like that?

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:40.300
You know? And it turns out like those can be fun.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:44.580
Um, but yeah, this whole series is brand new to me.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:46.680
Um, including this NES game.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.120
I had never touched it before.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:50.260
How about you? I hadn't played this.

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:52.200
I hadn't even played the Xbox version.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:03:01.040
All I know of the Xbox version is that it had laughably over the top cut scenes, um, uh, and, and characterizations.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:05.700
Um, but yeah, this is my first exposure to Ninja Gaiden in general.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:14.300
And, you know, when we were playing, uh, Castlevania II, Simon's Quest a while back, that was another game that had a reputation to it.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:25.780
And I think we all came to the conclusion of like, you know, isn't this weird that like this and Zelda II are coming out around the same time and they have like similar gameplay styles.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:32.960
Uh, of course, uh, of course, Castlevania II, you know, it like, it beat it here in the States, but it actually came out long after in Japan.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.760
So, uh, it was technically copying Zelda II.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:42.800
Here, I was very surprised to see how much, uh, of Ninja Gaiden is really just Castlevania I.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:49.260
You know, I didn't actually put that together, but I, I kind of get what you're saying there.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:55.200
Um, I feel like the movement in this game is really what sets it apart.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:04:10.400
Um, there, there's definitely some parts of Castlevania I, uh, in terms of its controls and like, uh, the speed of the movement and some of the sticky shit with that, um, that I think feels a little bit better in this game.

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:18.420
Uh, but in terms of like the general layout and the, and, uh, and like the, the general structure, I, I do agree.

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:21.040
Yeah. I could see a lot of, a lot of Castlevania in this.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:21.940
It's pretty crazy.

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:25.760
Like you look at the UI and it's almost like one-to-one the same.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:28.500
Uh, there's, there's bats in this game.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:36.100
There's, there's these little guys who are like hunched and then they, all of a sudden they just like spring out into action and attack you.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:42.180
It reminds me of those, uh, same like characters that go up against you in the Frankenstein level of Castlevania.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:45.780
I just think it's like, it's just insane how many parallels there are.

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:50.320
And I think most of what you're going to hear me say in this episode are improvements.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.320
I would also apply to Castlevania.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:54.720
Um, but it's no surprise.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:58.020
Castlevania is my favorite NES game so far.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:03.000
So I think like, you know, Ninja Gaiden copying the formula might not hurt it.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:04.400
I just wasn't expecting it.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:09.700
Yeah. Um, for some reason, I don't know if I'm thinking of the right game series.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:15.200
Um, what I was expecting from this game was one hit KO.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:20.260
Is that Shinobi or is that like a Ninja Gaiden thing?

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:23.260
No, that's a, that's, that's not a Ninja Gaiden thing.

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:25.460
So I don't know if that's a Shinobi thing.

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:26.440
I never played Shinobi.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:28.280
That's Sega's Ninja series.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:32.700
But, um, I'm surprised, you know, the, the one hit thing.

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:35.240
And I remember we talked about that in a, in a previous episode too.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:40.520
Um, that would like, to me, that would explain why people think this game is so difficult.

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:46.840
That's sort of what made me think of why I never wanted to play the fricking new ones is because I felt like, oh, one hit, you're dead.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:50.240
Uh, but, um, once again,

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:59.060
we're sort of experiencing these games differently than their legacy would suggest, um, in previous episodes.

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:27.700
And so I'm not really sure where you want to start when you talk about, uh, Ninja Gaiden here, because, uh, you know, you get right into the gameplay and, and everything that that has to offer.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:35.580
But I think that before all of that, there's also just a, a presentation element to the game, uh, that lets you know.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:43.220
And I think we talked about this in a previous episode too, of like, sometimes you play a game and you know that it's going to be like a good time.

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:45.640
Uh, especially on these earlier games.

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:51.700
Cause right away, like based on the way that the character feels or the way that the game is, uh, is drawn out.

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:54.320
Like you can tell like, ah, I'm not going to really like this.

00:06:54.440 --> 00:07:01.560
Something about the very start of this game and the way it handled itself, like immediately, let me know, like, I'm probably going to enjoy this.

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:15.820
Did you feel that? Uh, yeah, I would say that the, um, the, where I want to start is the presentation, uh, because when I read the manual for this, I was, I was very enthused to read that they have like, what was it called?

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:19.200
Like Tecmo, uh, theater or something.

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:22.140
Is it Tecmo? Um, I, I forget.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:24.640
Yes, it is Tecmo, but I forget what they, um,

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:26.340
Yeah, they called it Tecmo Theater.

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:28.440
They actually copyrighted that term.

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:31.540
Yeah. And it's just like their word for cutscenes.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.540
And I really appreciate these cutscenes.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:46.620
They're, um, I think they've, they feel a little bit better than even like Golgo 13, which so far is sort of like the, um, I find the best cutscenes so far.

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:50.020
Um, especially better than Rambo.

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:53.060
Um, and it actually seems to tell a coherent story.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:56.780
I don't know how much it's sort of related to the gameplay.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:08:01.420
It seems like the story is sort of happening in a different world than the gameplay.

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:05.200
But, um, there, it's really great art.

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:07.340
Um, the music's fine.

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:16.000
Uh, I really, I really like the idea of a, of a guy in full ninja gear just sitting in an office in the CIA.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:18.520
Um, lots of great stuff here.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:22.640
Great animation from where there actually is animation.

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:29.300
It's over 20 minutes of cinematic cutscenes in an NES game, uh, which sounds crazy.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:32.380
But also, you can, you can skip all of this easily.

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:36.460
You don't have to watch these scenes, which is also like a nice breath of fresh air.

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:41.060
That's crazy. Yeah. You can just hit the start button and move on to the next level and it's like no big deal.

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:45.140
But the acts, uh, you know, there's six acts in the game.

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:49.420
They actually feel like 30 minute episodes of an anime, right?

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.720
Yeah, they got that feel to them.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:58.520
Uh, especially, um, because their length sort of shifts as the game goes on.

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:07.600
I feel like act one is like one level long and, uh, there's sort of more stuff going on in the later ones where there's more meat to the story.

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:11.240
Um, I, I really enjoyed these.

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:15.540
It was a really good, uh, reward for completing a level.

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:20.900
Yeah, it was unexpected when it first happened after the completion of the first level.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:23.200
I was, I was like, whoa, this is, this is happening.

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:26.000
Like, uh, we're actually going to like get some story and stuff.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:31.860
It's completely unnecessary, but, and like you said, it doesn't necessarily feel like it's happening in the same world.

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:33.520
Except for that really cool scene.

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:39.620
I think it's an act four or three where you get to like the end of the mountain and all of a sudden it cuts to a cut scene.

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:41.120
Oh yeah, yeah.

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:41.980
That felt cool.

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:44.380
That felt cinematic. Very, yeah, I agree.

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:52.400
Uh, is that where, is it the one that's sort of like the wide shot of, uh, finally discovering this giant mountain in the middle of the Amazon?

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:53.520
Yep, exactly.

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:58.160
Okay. That they could have just seen from the helicopter, but whatever.

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:02.560
And I guess I didn't really expect like that kind of world in Ninja Gaiden.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:05.360
I think I expected like not even that time period, right?

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:13.480
Like, did you expect, um, Ryu, who is the ninja, like, did you expect him to exist along the same time as like the CIA in America?

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:18.320
No, I had no idea that this game had anything to do with, uh, the West.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:22.820
I thought it was sort of going to take place in old timey Japan.

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:34.460
Well, allegedly, uh, according to the Tecmo developers, they actually made the game because in their own words, ninjas were having a renaissance in North America.

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:40.740
Like, I don't know if they are specifically calling out the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles, which are also becoming incredibly popular.

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:42.140
That's some great market research.

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:44.580
Just, you know what I mean? It's just the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles.

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:48.120
Well, there was probably a bunch of ninja blockbuster movies too, right?

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:57.440
Like, I gotta think that, um, I can't think of any off the top of my head, but even things like Karate Kid have to be helping, like, the idea of ninjas.

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:00.060
You know what? You're probably right.

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:06.100
I don't know. I just feel like ninjas, even early 90s, like, ninjas is like a big thing and it's not exclusive to turtles.

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:09.920
It's not. Um, no, I, I, I can see that.

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:16.340
I think when I, when you think back to the culture of the 80s, I think there's a lot of ninja themed stuff.

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:28.240
So you're right. But the whole game just has like a, you know, since we're still on presentation here, it does just have like an odd mishmash of, um, of enemies and, and vibes going on.

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:30.940
I mean, like football players kind of attack you.

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:32.240
It looks like, right?

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:33.560
Like, are those guys wearing helmets?

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:34.620
Like, am I crazy here?

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:36.760
They look, they look like football players.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:40.220
I can't tell what their artwork was in the manual though.

00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:41.560
And then there's boxers.

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:43.900
There's just guys who just want to box you.

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:45.840
It's like, who, who is this?

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:49.320
Did I see a priest that was throwing like crucifixes at you?

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:51.040
Or is that me just, I don't know.

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:56.280
Well, it, it, technically, I don't know if, I don't know why you jumped a priest because I'm pretty sure that's like a ghoul.

00:11:56.660 --> 00:11:58.500
Uh, but. Well, it's a ghoul priest.

00:11:58.500 --> 00:11:59.320
Like if you look at the face.

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:00.380
Yeah, it's a ghoul priest.

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:03.700
Um, which are normal in that area of America.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:09.680
Yeah. And, um, and there's just something, I think there's just something funny about that, but it didn't bother me at all.

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:12.260
Because like you said, like, you know, this is, it's like an anime.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:13.440
It's kind of silly.

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:15.080
The story's all over the place too.

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:18.520
It's like, you've killed your, your, you know, your father's been killed.

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:20.160
You've been captured by the CIA.

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:22.160
You don't know who this mysterious woman is.

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:24.380
Oh, your father hasn't been killed.

00:12:24.580 --> 00:12:28.300
Turns out he's been turned into the, you know, the big bad boss.

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:29.180
I didn't know that.

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:31.740
Oh, you didn't, oh, you didn't get to stage six.

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:38.520
I would just like to say that this game is very hard and I make no apologies for the fact that I did not make it to stage six.

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:44.540
All right. So before we, before we like break down the gameplay elements, we, let's talk about that.

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:46.120
Cause you're saying that the game is very hard.

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:50.740
I completely agree with you, but it, it happens in a weird way, right?

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:57.580
The game isn't actually hard and it is very enjoyable to, uh, to be Ryu and, uh, you know,

00:12:57.580 --> 00:13:02.540
hop onto the walls and hang onto the ledges and attack the enemies and get the cool power-ups.

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:03.940
Like that's all fun.

00:13:04.060 --> 00:13:05.860
And I don't think any of the enemies are unfair.

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:10.200
I think there's just a, a point in this game where they should have said, you know,

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:14.040
we really need to reevaluate if the enemies should just spawn in constantly.

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:19.700
That is the main issue with, with the, with the gameplay in this game is,

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:26.640
and, and we've, we've damned games for this, um, that have lesser qualities elsewhere.

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:32.160
Um, it, it's just, it makes some sections almost impossible.

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:39.100
Um, unless you, uh, play, play the game in a much more conservative way, which I don't think

00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:40.520
is necessarily a bad thing.

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:46.340
Um, and it's a little bit more strategic than just like holding down, right.

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:49.460
The right, uh, holding down, going to the right.

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:52.580
Um, but it, it's a little unintuitive.

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:59.440
Uh, I did end up getting better at this game as I played, like, like I would hope most people

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:05.620
would, but there were still a lot of places that I just, uh, that, that like respawn,

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:08.300
that just, it just would soft lock me in some ways.

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:11.600
Yeah, there needed to be a cap on number of enemies.

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:15.720
And I know there are people who have beaten this game who are going to disagree there,

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:22.060
but I think, you know, the, the, the fun part of beating any video game, not even just

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:24.120
NES games, isn't how hard they are.

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:27.100
It's how good it feels to beat those games.

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:31.720
And I don't know about you, Sean, but like, if I could have beaten this game, I absolutely

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:33.100
would have, I would have went for it.

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:34.760
Like I was having a great time with it.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:37.160
It just, it gets to a point.

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:44.380
It gets to a point. Uh, on act, on act five and definitely act six, where this thing wants you to like,

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:49.200
you know, I couldn't even imagine how I would land on the next ledge while the enemies are

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:51.560
all still there. And there's a bird trying to get me.

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:54.960
And I have, and I have tremendous knockback.

00:14:54.960 --> 00:15:00.380
Knockback. A thing that we complained a lot about in Castlevania, which again is here, you know, other games

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:04.620
have knockback too. But I think since we're, since we're talking about it here in Castlevania, we might as well

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:09.300
talk about it for Ninja Gaiden, uh, Gaiden, Gaidan, uh, whatever you want to say.

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:15.940
Gaiden. Uh, yeah, we've got to talk about it because the knockback decision feels like something

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:21.940
that is just a relic of like, well, you know, I can't imagine, I can't imagine the developers.

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:23.060
Let me phrase it another way.

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:27.560
I can't imagine anybody saying the knockback is going to help the player.

00:15:27.560 --> 00:15:29.600
It's only designed there to hurt you.

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:33.420
I think that, I think the game needs knockback.

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:40.020
I think most games that have this sort of design, like does need knockback or else things get

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:44.200
a little, a little easier in the, like balance gets thrown off in the other direction.

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:50.280
I just think that, uh, you need a longer period of invincibility.

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:53.560
We're getting into nitty gritty now, but I think you need a longer period of invincibility

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:59.460
after getting hit and getting knocked back and hopefully not falling into a pit so that

00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:06.780
you can, if you need to just run past that enemy on that platform, um, and just like,

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:10.760
like lick your wounds and just be thankful that you didn't lose a life.

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:17.540
Uh, I think that that's a pretty good compromise, uh, in terms of, uh, all the issues that we,

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:22.460
or all those problems that we can get into, uh, just by getting knocked back into, into

00:16:23.740 --> 00:16:24.740
gullies every time.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:30.340
